-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024
-- (deposited text: ../../registers/source-bundle/BA1994.txt) -- NOUNS ONLY.
-- This module holds DECLARE and nothing else: the things a witness of ordinary competence could testify to
-- (a fine, a term of imprisonment, a kind of person, a piece of apparatus, a service on a list).
-- Every other module of this encoding imports it. It has no rules and no directives.

-- A maximum term of imprisonment, in months (the Act gives years in most places and months in s 50(4)).
DECLARE `Imprisonment` IS ONE OF
    `no imprisonment is provided`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` HAS `months` IS A NUMBER

-- A further fine for a continuing offence: the Act's words are "for every day or part of a day during which
-- the offence continues after conviction".
DECLARE `Daily fine` IS ONE OF
    `no further daily fine is provided`
    `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Forfeiture` IS ONE OF
    `no forfeiture is provided`
    `the apparatus installed or found in the possession of the person convicted is forfeited to the Authority`
    `the unauthorised decoder is forfeited to the Authority`

-- What a section says a person may be made to suffer at most on conviction.
-- Where the Act says "a fine not exceeding $X or imprisonment not exceeding Y or both", each figure is a ceiling
-- and the court may impose either or both: the record holds the two ceilings, not a sentence.
DECLARE `Punishment` HAS
    `fine not exceeding` IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment` IS A `Imprisonment`
    `daily fine` IS A `Daily fine`
    `forfeiture` IS A `Forfeiture`

-- The kinds of person that the Act's offence and licence provisions tell apart.
DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`
    `an unincorporated association other than a partnership`
    `a partnership`

-- The three licences the Act itself names (s 2(1), s 5(1), s 9).
DECLARE `Kind of licence` IS ONE OF
    `a broadcasting licence granted under section 8`
    `a class licence determined under section 9`
    `a broadcasting apparatus licence granted under section 20`

-- Apparatus, as a person could describe it: what it can receive and from where.
-- The two facts are the Act's own words in the definition of "broadcasting apparatus" (s 2(1)) and in the
-- interpretation paragraph of the First Schedule.
DECLARE `Apparatus` HAS
    `capable of reception of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `capable of direct reception from a satellite` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The services listed in the Second Schedule, in the Schedule's own order (items 1 to 20).
DECLARE `Second Schedule service` IS ONE OF
    `free-to-air nationwide television services`
    `free-to-air localised television services`
    `free-to-air international television services`
    `subscription nationwide television services`
    `subscription localised television services`
    `subscription international television services`
    `special interest television services`
    `free-to-air nationwide radio services`
    `free-to-air localised radio services`
    `free-to-air international radio services`
    `subscription nationwide radio services`
    `subscription localised radio services`
    `subscription international radio services`
    `special interest radio services`
    `audiotext services`
    `videotext services`
    `teletext services`
    `video-on-demand services`
    `broadcast data services`
    `computer online services`

-- What a person doing something with apparatus can say they did (s 20(1)(a) to (c)).
-- Paragraph (c) is "operate or have on any premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person broadcasting apparatus on or by which broadcasting services are received" (fork F-BA-03):
-- three facts, so that both readings of the premises phrase can be written: whether the person operates it, whether the person has it, and whether the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person.
DECLARE `Dealing with apparatus` HAS
    `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `operates it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What a person can be said to do with a decoder (s 48(1)): the nine acts the subsection lists.
DECLARE `Act with a decoder` IS ONE OF
    `manufacture`
    `assemble`
    `modify`
    `import`
    `export`
    `sell`
    `offer for sale`
    `let for hire`
    `otherwise distribute`

-- The ways s 64 lets a document be served (ss 64(2) to (5)).
DECLARE `Way to serve a document` IS ONE OF
    `give it personally to the individual, or to a partner, secretary or other similar officer, or manager`
    `leave it at, or send it by prepaid registered post to, the address the section names`
    `leave it with an adult apparently resident or employed at the individual's address`
    `affix a copy in a conspicuous place at the individual's address`
    `send it by fax`
    `send it by email`
    `give an electronic notice by the addressee's chosen means of notification`
    `post it on the website the Minister prescribed`
    `use another method the regulations authorise, with the addressee's consent`

-- Receiving equipment, described by what a witness could say about it, in the words the First Schedule and section 2(1) use in every vintage.
-- Section 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus": "any apparatus capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting service and specified in the First Schedule";
-- the two limbs "capable of" and "designed or constructed for" are kept apart so that both readings of the definition (fork F-BA-01) can be written.
-- The First Schedule's items, in the Revised Editions 2003 and 2012: "broadcast television receiver" (any apparatus used for the visual and aural reception in monochrome or colour
-- of any broadcasting service), "broadcast sound receiver" (any apparatus used for the aural reception of any broadcasting service) and the TVRO system (capable of direct reception from a satellite).
DECLARE `Receiving equipment` HAS
    `capable of the reception of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service in monochrome or colour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `capable of direct reception of a broadcasting service from a satellite` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A version of the First Schedule. Every version has TWO dates.
-- `takes effect on` is the day the text is the law for conduct (VALID TIME: on an unstable build, `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` or `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`).
-- `published on` is the day the text was made known to a reader (RULE-VERSION TIME: on an unstable build, the rule-version axis, `tcRuleVersionTime`).
-- A question is asked with two days, the day of the conduct and the day the law is read as at; the version read is the latest published on or before the reading day
-- among those that take effect on or before the day of the conduct. Build 98 of `main` rejects those built-ins, so both days are ordinary inputs and the versions are a table.
DECLARE `First Schedule version` HAS
    `source` IS A STRING
    `takes effect on` IS A DATE
    `published on` IS A DATE
    `lists broadcast television receivers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lists broadcast sound receivers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lists TVRO systems` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A version of the Third Schedule (relevant licensable broadcasting service, section 31(6)), with the same two dates.
DECLARE `Third Schedule version` HAS
    `source` IS A STRING
    `takes effect on` IS A DATE
    `published on` IS A DATE
    `providers of the subscription nationwide television service` IS A LIST OF STRING

-- One text of a provision (or of an instrument), with the two days the two-date model reads it by.
-- `is the text after the amendment` is FALSE for the text before the amending Act or Order and TRUE for the text it made.
DECLARE `Provision text version` HAS
    `source` IS A STRING
    `takes effect on` IS A DATE
    `published on` IS A DATE
    `is the text after the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A version of the Television and Radio Licensing Regulations (Rg 1), with the same two dates as a Schedule version.
-- `the text read` says which: "RevEd 2004" (the Revised Edition of 29 February 2004), "amended by S 333/2004" or "revoked by S 548/2012".
DECLARE `Rg 1 version` HAS
    `source` IS A STRING
    `the text read` IS A STRING
    `takes effect on` IS A DATE
    `published on` IS A DATE
    `the Regulations are in force` IS A BOOLEAN
